**Original write-up (2026-09), kept for the record — root cause below was
correct; see the UPDATE above for the fix.**

A real client's `com.canonical.dbusmenu.GetLayout` call (confirmed with both
`gnome-panel`'s real `IndicatorAppletComplete` widget and, isolated and
reproduced on demand, plain `dbus-send`) reliably disconnected
`ownConnection` mid-reply — `dbus-monitor` showed `NoReply: "Message
recipient disconnected from message bus without replying"` every time, and
`gnome-panel`'s own log independently confirmed it: `LIBDBUSMENU-GLIB
-WARNING: Getting layout failed: Operation was cancelled`. `Properties
.GetAll` and `GetGroupProperties` against the exact same connection did NOT
reproduce this — it was specific to `GetLayout`'s reply. Root cause: the
wire-marshalling gap `DBusMenuLayoutBuilder.layout(items:)`'s own doc
comment already flagged (`DBusValue.array([]).signatureCode` degrading an
EMPTY array to `"ay"` instead of the semantically-correct `"a{sv}"`/`"av"`
— `GetLayout`'s root item always has empty `properties`/leaf `children`,
`GetGroupProperties`'s reply never does for a real, populated menu, which is
exactly why one reproduced this and the other didn't).

A second, smaller gap found the same way: `StatusNotifierRequest.decode`'s
`org.freedesktop.DBus.Properties` case never checks `message.path`, so a
`Properties.GetAll` aimed at `/app/clipnest/TrayMenu` (which should answer
`com.canonical.dbusmenu`'s OWN properties — `Version`/`TextDirection`/
`Status`/`IconThemePath`) is answered with the `StatusNotifierItem`'s SNI
properties instead (confirmed live: `gnome-panel`'s widget receives
`Category`/`Id`/`Title`/... where it asked for the menu's own properties).
Not fixed here either — out of this task's assigned scope
(`Hello`/identity/`GetGroupProperties`).

Known gap #5 (P0, real, verified, NOT fixable from this package's Swift
source — needs a dependency version bump)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Any external X11 client that becomes the `CLIPBOARD` selection owner while
GTK's own async `TARGETS` negotiation with it hits a specific, benign ICCCM
edge case (its `SelectionNotify` reply property doesn't land on GDK's
window — reproduced with a raw `python-xlib` client that answers correctly
but writes the property to its own window instead of the requestor's; no
malice required) crashes the WHOLE `clipnest` process with a `SIGSEGV`.
Root-caused with a fully-symbolicated `gdb` backtrace against this series'
actual `libgtk-4-1`/`libglib2.0-0` (installed matching `-dbgsym` ddebs):
`strcmp`←`g_str_equal(type=NULL,"ATOM")`←
`gdk_x11_clipboard_request_targets_got_stream`
(`gdk/x11/gdkclipboard-x11.c`) — a NULL-unsafe string compare GTK itself
fixed later (switched to the NULL-safe `g_strcmp0`) in a clipboard/selection
rewrite landing around GTK 4.10 (upstream commit `0212291a`). Ubuntu 22.04's
own archives (`main`, `-updates`, `-security`) top out at the AFFECTED
`4.6.9+ds-0ubuntu0.22.04.2` — there is no newer `libgtk-4-1` to `apt install`
on this series. Confirmed via source (`gdk/x11/gdkdisplay-x11.c`'s
`_gdk_x11_display_open`) that GTK creates its own, independent CLIPBOARD/
PRIMARY tracking UNCONDITIONALLY the instant `gtk_init()` opens a display —
before any of this app's code runs, with no `GDK_DEBUG`/`GDK_DISABLE` flag
or supported API to opt out — so this is not fixable by changing how
`ClipnestGTK`/`ClipnestPlatformLinux` use GTK's clipboard APIs. **The real
fix is a `libgtk-4-1` version bump** (>= the point release carrying commit
`0212291a`) via a GNOME/Ubuntu PPA backport pinned in this image's build
stage (and eventually `debian/control`'s `Build-Depends`/generated
`${shlibs:Depends}`), or building GTK4 from source — tracked as task
`T-WB1-GTKBUMP` in `.claude/task-board.md`, `.claude/project-context.md`'s
decision D81 has the full root-cause trail (source line numbers + the exact
core-dump backtrace). Not fixed in this file/session — packaging-level,
outside a Swift source change's reach.
